# Every page here is generated, and the export runs from two machines: macOS
# writes LF, the Windows weekly sync writes CRLF. Without normalisation whichever
# one published last rewrote every line of every file, burying a two-line pick
# change under thousands of line-ending diffs. Normalise on the way into git so a
# diff shows only what actually changed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# iCalendar mandates CRLF (RFC 5545 s3.1) and export_draft_calendar.py writes it
# deliberately with newline="\r\n". GitHub Pages serves the committed bytes, so
# the blob itself has to keep them -- `text eol=crlf` would still store LF and
# serve LF. -text keeps git's hands off entirely.
*.ics -text

# Fonts are binary. A CRLF byte pair inside one is data, not a line ending, and
# "normalising" it silently corrupts the file -- which is exactly how a byte went
# missing from both Barlow faces before this file existed.
*.woff2 binary
